{"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Tutorials","title":"Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/Tutorial-TestingFlows"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/innoroutertesting"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterMacros"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/InnoRouterTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"InnoRouterTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ships three test stores that mirror the production stores’ public API and transparently subscribe to every public observation callback:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationTestStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — asserts "},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" events (push\/pop\/batch\/transaction\/middleware mutation\/path mismatch)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ModalTestStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — asserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"ModalStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" events (present\/dismiss\/queue\/intercept\/middleware mutation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"FlowTestStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — asserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"FlowStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" intents end-to-end, including the inner navigation and modal emissions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"@testable import","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is required. The harness itself avoids app-side access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to FlowStore internals; configure inner navigation \/ modal behavior through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FlowStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Event-queue-model","text":"Event queue model","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each test store owns a FIFO queue. Every time the underlying store emits an observation callback, the corresponding event is appended. Tests consume events in order via "},{"code":"receive(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or its typed helpers ("},{"code":"receiveChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"receivePresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"receiveIntentRejected","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on). A strict-mode test store fails via Swift Testing "},{"code":"Issue.record","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if any events are left unasserted at deinit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["import Testing","import InnoRouterTesting","","@Test","@MainActor","func pushHomeLogsChangeEvent() {","    let store = NavigationTestStore<AppRoute>()","    store.send(.push(.home))","    store.receiveChange { old, new in","        old.path.isEmpty && new.path == [.home]","    }","    store.finish()","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Exhaustivity","text":"Exhaustivity","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default mode is ","type":"text"},{"code":"TestExhaustivity.strict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": unasserted events at store deinit (or at an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"finish()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are reported as test issues. ","type":"text"},{"code":"TestExhaustivity.off","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preserves the ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" assertions but silences the final drain check — useful when incrementally migrating large legacy suites.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"User-callbacks-are-preserved","text":"User callbacks are preserved","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you pass a production ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ModalStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"FlowStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into a test store, every hook (including ","type":"text"},{"code":"onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCommandIntercepted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onPathMismatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", etc.) still fires. The test store appends events after the user callback runs, so production middleware and analytics pipelines behave under test exactly as they would in the app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"End-to-end-flow-assertions","text":"End-to-end flow assertions","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowTestStore"},{"text":" subscribes to the inner ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalStore"},{"text":"’s full observation surface and wraps those emissions into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigation(...)"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".modal(...)"},{"text":" events on a single queue. This lets a test assert the complete chain triggered by one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowIntent"},{"text":" — for instance, that a sheet-blocking middleware prevents the inner navigation store from seeing any command:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let store = FlowTestStore<AppRoute>(","    configuration: FlowStoreConfiguration(","        modal: ModalStoreConfiguration(","            middlewares: [","                ModalMiddlewareRegistration(","                    middleware: BlockSheetMiddleware(),","                    debugName: \"BlockSheet\"","                )","            ]","        )","    )",")","","store.send(.presentSheet(.onboarding))","store.receiveIntentRejected(","    intent: .presentSheet(.onboarding),","    reason: .middlewareRejected(debugName: \"BlockSheet\")",")","store.expectNoMoreEvents()"],"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Host-less, Swift-Testing native assertion harness for InnoRouter’s navigation, modal, and flow authorities.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"InnoRouterMacros"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"InnoRouterTesting"},"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing/documentation/InnoRouterMacros":{"title":"InnoRouterMacros","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterMacros","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/innoroutermacros"},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing/documentation/InnoRouterTesting/Tutorial-TestingFlows":{"title":"Testing Flows End-to-End with `FlowTestStore`","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/tutorial-testingflows","abstract":[{"text":"Assert the complete chain triggered by a single ","type":"text"},{"code":"FlowIntent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"navigation, modal, middleware cancellation, path reconciliation —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through a single FIFO receive queue, without mounting any SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/Tutorial-TestingFl